          "derivation": "New Persian ژرف žarf 'deep' (with the abstract ژرفا žarfā 'depth', formed with the -ā suffix as in پهنا, درازا) continues the Middle Iranian word by metathesis of the cluster: Old/Middle Iranian -fr- > NP -rf-, exactly the change Hübschmann sets out as a sound law (Persische Studien p.266, §c: 'Ap. fr ~ np. rf: barf \"Schnee\" = phl. vafr = zd. vafra-; žarf \"tief\" = zd. jafra-'). Horn (no. 685) gives žerf and Judaeo-Persian ژרף (Isaiah 29:15). The initial ž- (rather than z-) points to the Parthian/Northwestern form žafr rather than to Book Pahlavi zofr. Ferdowsī's line quoted in the chart, یکی ژرف دریاست بن ناپدید / در گنج رازش ندارد کلید, is the same verse Mo'in prints in his footnote to Borhan-e Qāṭeʿ. Nourai's chain Av. jafra > MIr. žafr/zafr > NP žarf is the standard account.",
